"""Pinned external-market ids for the 237 Predictions Cup markets (data only, no logic).

Generated offline from the scout's table (scratchpad ``paper/fixtures/supermarket_titles.txt``),
which merges other participants' public mapping files (all accessed 2026-10-04):

* Polymarket "<Race> Election Winner" market ids and labels: github.com/grissou/prediction-market-maker
  ``ref_map.json`` (commit a49587c); CA-22 from github.com/DanielCWeng/predictions-cup (fb4f6c6).
* Kalshi tickers: github.com/christiano7777777/sig-arb-bot ``kalshi_map.json`` (a209d57); chamber-control
  tickers from github.com/nullif1ed/sigprediction ``lib/core/races.ts``.
* Super Market market / exchange ids and titles: DanielCWeng ``sig_polymarket_2026.csv``.

These are other students' work. ``fairvalue`` treats every pin as a *candidate* and re-validates
it against live data before use (active, not closed, a 2026 event, the party tag matches); a pin
that fails validation is dropped, never guessed. Rows are keyed by ``(race_key, party)``; the
Super Market ids are only a cross-check (match by parsed title, never by id).

Revision 2: the Kentucky Senate rows were pinned to ``SENATELA-26-D/R`` (the Louisiana race) in the
source file; those two Kalshi pins are blanked (provably wrong, not guessed), leaving 220 Kalshi pins.

Columns: race_key, party, polymarket_market_id ("" = none), polymarket_label, kalshi_ticker
("" = none), match_kind ("EXACT" | "NEAR": chamber control and Independent legs settle on
different wording), sig_market_id, sig_exchange_id, sig_title.
"""

